       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum daily dose of metformin is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2000 mg/day** for extended-release, so this order is twice the maximum. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release). 1700 mg is twice 850 mg, so this may be what was meant.\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth twice daily** (1700 mg/day total), if 1700 mg was meant as the total daily dose.\n- Another dose. If the patient is just starting metformin, the usual approach is 500 mg once or twice daily, increased slowly.\n\nPlease tell me the dose you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release, and I'll enter it. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a reason, and I'll include it in a note on the order. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
