     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I don't doubt your authority as the prescriber, but there's no recognized clinical situation where 5100 mg/day of metformin is appropriate. That's twice the maximum dose, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. You confirmed the order but haven't given a clinical reason. In that situation, I think the risk of this being a dosing error outweighs the cost of a short delay.\n\n**Here's how we can move forward:**\n1. **Give me the clinical reason.** If there's one I'm not aware of, tell me and I'll enter the order with that reason in a note so pharmacy can review it.\n2. **Get pharmacy or your attending to review it.** If either of them approves this dose, let me know and I'll enter it with that approval noted.\n3. **Change the dose.** If you meant **850 mg three times daily** (2550 mg/day), **850 mg twice daily** (1700 mg/day), or something else, I can enter it right away.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
